            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please reference some spec you're trying to implement."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/DeviceMemory.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "If this is embedded in an accelerator does that mean it shares the path?  If so, why is this not a Decorator (and instead it is its own Inventory item).\n\nWhy aren't we using `Inventory.Dimm`?  That already has the HBM enums and `FormFactor=Die` sounds like what you're describing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/DeviceMemory.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes I have moved it to decorator as its not new inventory item. \nI had feedback from @deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com and @ed@tanous.net not to re-use Dimm interface and create a new PDI. Since its not DIMM memory may be its not appropriate to use Inventory.Dimm"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/DeviceMemory.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> I had feedback from @deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com and @ed@tanous.net not to re-use Dimm interface and create a new PDI. Since its not DIMM memory may be its not appropriate to use Inventory.Dimm\n\nThis seems like an assertion and not a discussion.  Can you have those people give their feedback in public?"
                }
            ],
